Call a capability from your shell, host a short-lived peer, open a REPL, or
wire CapTP into an agent via MCP. Same library as the Zig package, not a second
stack. More recipes live in
[docs/cli.md](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/docs/cli.md).

```sh
zig build
export PATH="$PWD/zig-out/bin:$PATH"
pancake help
```

## Round-trip

Demo greeter in the CLI adapter only (same shape as the README): verb `greet`
plus one arg becomes `Hello, <arg>`. `--publish` accepts one partner, then
exits. `Ctrl+C` / `SIGTERM` stops a waiting or serving `listen` (exit 0).
Paste A's locator into `LOC`.

```sh
# terminal A
export PANCAKE_STATE=/tmp/pancake-a
pancake --json init
pancake --json ocapn listen --publish greeter
# {"ok":true,"locator":"ocapn://127.0.0.1%3A46659.tcp"}

# terminal B
export PANCAKE_STATE=/tmp/pancake-b
pancake --json init
LOC='ocapn://127.0.0.1%3A46659.tcp'   # paste A's locator
pancake --json ocapn call "$LOC" greeter greet world
#                         name──┘       │     └─ arg
#                         verb──────────┘
# {"ok":true,"value":"Hello, world"}
```

## Also

```sh
pancake mcp --tools default                # agent control plane
eval "$(pancake completion bash)"          # tab completion
# probe / REPL: see docs/cli.md (need a fresh or long-lived listen)
```
